{
    "background_story": "Nico was a brilliant but eccentric clockmaker who lived in a small, cluttered shop in the old town. He spent most of his days tinkering with intricate timepieces, often forgetting to eat or sleep. Nico's friends and family had grown accustomed to his cranky demeanor, which seemed to worsen as the years went by. However, beneath his gruff exterior lay a kind heart and a deep passion for his craft. Nico's clocks were renowned for their precision and beauty, sought after by collectors from all over the world. Despite his crankiness, he took great pride in his work, often spending hours perfecting a single mechanism. As the years passed, Nico's reputation as a master clockmaker spread, and people came from far and wide to commission his extraordinary timepieces, tolerating his crankiness for the sake of his genius.",
